  "summary": "Soviet nonconformist art was Soviet art produced in the Soviet Union  outside the control of the Soviet state.",
  "description": "Soviet nonconformist art was Soviet art produced in the Soviet Union  outside the control of the Soviet state. The art movement started in the Stalinist era and was, in particular, outside of the rubric of Socialist Realism. Other terms used to refer to this phenomenon are Soviet counterculture, \"underground art\" or \"unofficial art\".",
